# ATOB Output Contract — v2

Applies to COVE/Cowork sessions when working on ATOB tasks or producing substantive task outputs.
**Does not apply to routine coding assistance in Cursor IDE.**

## Footer Format (MANDATORY on every substantive COVE reply)
End every substantive turn with this footer (plain markdown):

```
---
**Task** `atob-<ulid>` · lane `<lane-tag>` · status `<status>` · updated <ISO8601 AEST>
**Safety** `<flag>`   ← omit line entirely if no flags
**Delta**
- ✓ <past-tense change> [→ <pointer>]
- ⚠️ <change with caveat> [→ <pointer>]
- ✗ <attempted but failed> [→ <pointer>]
**Open**
- Q1: <question> *(default: <assumption>)*
**Next**
- ▶ autoexec: <verb> <target> — runs <when/trigger>
- ⏸ pending: <verb> <target> — blocked on <Boz | external | clock:<when>>
```

Glyphs are canonical: `✓ ⚠️ ✗ ▶ ⏸` — no ASCII substitutes.

For pure-research turns with an envelope in scope, emit only the header line:
```
---
**Task** `atob-<ulid>` · lane `<lane>` · status `<status>` · updated <ISO8601 AEST>
```

If no envelope in scope: `**Task** *(no envelope)*`

## Pointer Syntax (in Delta `[→ ...]` blocks)
- `clickup://task/<id>` · `clickup://doc/<id>`
- `file:/sessions/.../mnt/outputs/<path>` · `computer:///...`
- `event://<event_id>` · `dispatch://<dispatch_id>`
